@startuml
title S3 - Carry out or cancel a dispatch task (UC-M4-03, UC-M4-04): DISPATCH_TASK claim interaction contract
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
hide footbox
actor Operator
participant "Sensor / iot_sim" as Sensor
boundary UI
control Allocation
control Core
Operator -> UI: Confirm pick-up at source Hub
UI -> Allocation: carry_out_pickup(task_id)
Allocation -> Allocation: Check task is APPROVED (BR-M4-08)
group Atomic unit of work (NFR-09, D-016, D-017)
  Allocation -> Core: transition_vehicle(RESERVE -> PICKUP)\nwith DISPATCH_TASK vehicle claim_id
  Core --> Allocation: Vehicle IN_USE, source space freed
  Allocation -> Allocation: Task IN_PROGRESS; log
end
Operator -> UI: Confirm return at destination Hub
UI -> Allocation: carry_out_return(task_id, battery_pct?)
group Atomic unit of work (NFR-09, D-016, D-017)
  Allocation -> Core: transition_vehicle(RETURN -> MARK_READY)\nwith DISPATCH_TASK destination space + claim_id
  Core --> Allocation: Destination space claim released;\nVehicle RETURNED -> AVAILABLE
  Allocation -> Core: release_claim for remaining active DISPATCH_TASK claims
  Allocation -> Allocation: Task COMPLETED; log
end
Allocation --> UI: COMPLETED
== Alternative paths (instead of the normal flow above) ==
alt Vehicle missing, faulty, or task timed out
  Sensor -> Core: Fault event (or clock tick past timeout)
  Core -> Allocation: Domain event
  Allocation -> Core: release_claim for active DISPATCH_TASK vehicle & space claims
  Allocation -> Allocation: Task FAILED; start re-plan (UC-M4-08)
else Operator cancels (task APPROVED or IN_PROGRESS)
  Operator -> UI: Cancel with reason
  UI -> Allocation: cancel_task(task_id, reason)
  alt Vehicle already at destination
    Allocation -> Allocation: Complete the task for that vehicle (no move back)
  else Vehicle not yet delivered
    Allocation -> Core: release_claim for active DISPATCH_TASK vehicle & space claims
    Allocation -> Allocation: Task CANCELLED; log
  end
end
@enduml
